      {
        "id": 159438,
        "name": "mlangsdorf",
        "username": "mlangsdorf",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/c4cdca/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-02-10T00:29:06.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I tried going the double Takedown route, but didn't quite manage to do enough damage to the Drums before Gloomie flipped. As it turns out, the combination of stun bolts, neurotoxin darts, Fortitude, Lead From the Front, Smoke Bombs, Heavy Plating, and Atlantean Throne Room was enough to prevent Gloomweaver or his wretched Cursed Acolyte from doing any damage to anyone, which meant that Chrono-Ranger could safely play Hunter Hunted and then Danny-Boy did everything in sight for 4-6 points of damage every turn. He just blew everything apart, and then Haka finished with a Rampage. Bunker had 6 cards on his Omni-Cannon in case anything went wrong. Ended with everyone above 23 HP.</p><p>Pretty straightforward game. Thanks to Servoret for reminding me that Neurotoxin Dart Thrower exists; I would have pulled Masada early and taken more damage and would have been sad.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
